  "budget": 0.75,
  "budgetReason": "The API gives a check only a name and a count, so three things the board draws have no data: the second line under each failed check, the fix button's own words (\"Go to question 4\") and the unit after a count (\"214 facts\"). They are 0.55% of the screen; the shared case bar adds 0.14%.",
  "deviations": [
    "A failed check shows \"Fix it\" and, from its count, \"2 found\" where the board has a sentence of detail and a named button: the API sends no detail or label (gap).",
    "A passed check shows its count as a bare number; the board adds a unit (\"214 facts\") and, for two rows, \"214 of 214\" (gap).",
    "The ring's \"of 28\" is 17px, the board's 14px (nfr U2).",
    "\"Check again\" is a link the board omits; it is removed from the page for the comparison.",
    "The board draws only the failed state; the passed state (all clear, \"Sign and send\" on) has no board and keeps its existing layout.",
    "Hit areas are real boxes, not a ::after: every button and link is 52px tall as the 52px rule and the e2e check measure it. Links keep the board's text position (padding that a negative margin takes back); drawn chips and pills are taller than the board by the difference. Probes: see all, spot link differ in height/position only."
  ]
